Attribution and prior work
--------------------------

Some of this material is adapted, and the licence above is partly inherited
rather than merely chosen.  ShareAlike requires a derivative to carry the
same licence as its source, so CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 is the obligation here as
well as the preference:

  tutorials/jupyter_basics.org, sections 1-3
      Adapted from EEP153 (Materials/Project0/python_intro_1.ipynb), which
      is CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 and which in turn credits Berkeley's Data 8 course
      for the same material.  Both attributions are kept in the tutorial
      text itself; please keep them in any further adaptation.

Everything else here -- lectures.org and the notebooks and slides generated
from it, the other two tutorials, the GLSS7 exercise, and the workshop site
-- is original to this repository.

The survey microdata is NOT covered by this licence.  World Bank LSMS data
cannot be freely redistributed; the workshop works from harmonized derived
extracts, and participants who want raw access register for their own free
World Bank Microdata keys.  See the workshop site for details.
